Article 26 Units or individuals that meet any of the following conditions shall be rewarded by the education administrative department and relevant departments:
(1) those that have achieved significant results in improving the conditions for running a kindergarten;
(2) those that have achieved significant results in nursing care and education work;
(3) those that have achieved significant results in kindergarten administration work.

Article 27 A kindergarten that violates these Regulations and is under any of the following circumstances shall be subject to an administrative penalty of being ordered to rectify within a time limit, suspension of enrollment, or suspension of operation by the education administrative department depending on the seriousness of the circumstances:
(1) enrolling children without registration;
(2) having premises and facilities that do not meet the national hygiene standards or safety standards, harming children's health or threatening children's lives;
(3) adopting educational contents and methods that violate the laws of preschool education and harm children's physical and mental health.

Article 28 A unit or individual that violates these Regulations and is under any of the following circumstances shall be subject to an administrative penalty of a warning or a fine imposed by the education administrative department on the person directly responsible, or the education administrative department shall suggest that the relevant department impose an administrative sanction on the responsible person:
(1) subjecting children to corporal punishment or disguised corporal punishment;
(2) using toxic or harmful substances to make teaching aids or toys;
(3) deducting or misappropriating kindergarten funds;
(4) encroaching upon or damaging kindergarten premises or equipment;
(5) disrupting the normal work order of a kindergarten;
(6) setting up buildings or facilities around a kindergarten that are dangerous, polluting, or that affect the kindergarten's lighting.
Where the circumstances mentioned in the preceding paragraph are serious and constitute a crime, the judicial authority shall investigate criminal liability according to law.
